Package: flatr
Title: Objective Bayes for Linear Regression with the Flat-R Prior
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Diemithry M.", "Kloppenburg", email = "diemithrykloppenburg@hotmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Bayes factors and estimation for linear regression with a prior
    that is flat on the multiple correlation R for any number of predictors,
    with every way of dividing the explained variance over the predictors
    equally plausible. It is a mixture of Zellner g-priors whose implied prior
    on R-squared, Beta(1/2, 1), does not change with the number of predictors;
    with one predictor it is Jeffreys' flat prior on the correlation. Bayes
    factors between any two linear models come from a closed form that needs
    only R-squared, n and k. Estimation samples the prior in its own
    coordinates (R and a direction) with Stan. Every function also offers the
    uniform-correlations prior (every correlation matrix of the outcome and
    predictors equally likely, R-squared ~ Beta(k/2, 1), as rstanarm stan_lm
    with eta = 1), under which each coefficient's partial correlation is flat.
